---
// The site's navigation: only pages that exist. Explore the trail (Phase 4)
// and Get involved (Phase 6) join this row when they are real - WEBSITE.md §9
// sequences them - and not a day before: a nav link to a page that is not
// there is a promise the site breaks on its second click.
//
// FOR ORGS IS NOW REAL, so it joined the row (features/ORG_ONBOARDING.md,
// #116's Phase 6). The condition above is the reason it took this long and is
// the reason the other two are still absent: /for-orgs/ exists, it answers,
// and the rule is satisfied rather than waived.
//
// IT SAYS "ORG" AND NOT "CLUB" since 2026-09-17, matching the design handoff,
// the console and every route. ORG_ONBOARDING.md's conflict 2 is the
// argument: not every organization that maintains a trail is a club - OPRHP
// is a state agency, Mohonk a preserve, a land trust neither - and the site
// was the last surface still saying the narrower word.
//
// THE CTA IS THE DESIGN'S. This row carried `Support the trail`, on the
// reasoning that an organization arriving should not outrank a hiker
// donating. The maintainer decided the other way on 2026-09-17, against the
// handoff's own nav: an organization that has come this far is the visitor
// this row should serve, and `Add your trails` is what the design puts here.
import Mark from './Mark.astro'

const here = Astro.url.pathname
const links = [
  { href: '/get-the-app/', label: 'Get the app' },
  { href: '/for-orgs/', label: 'For orgs' },
  { href: '/about/', label: 'About' },
]
---

<nav class="wrap nav" aria-label="Site">
  <a class="nav__brand" href="/">
    <Mark id="nav-mark" size={34} />
    <span class="nav__word">OurHike</span>
  </a>
  {
    links.map((link) => (
      <a
        class="nav__link"
        href={link.href}
        aria-current={here === link.href ? 'page' : undefined}
      >
        {link.label}
      </a>
    ))
  }
  <a
    class="nav__cta"
    href="/for-orgs/"
    aria-current={here === '/for-orgs/' ? 'page' : undefined}
  >
    Add your trails
  </a>
</nav>
